== Title decisions ==

* '''[[Predicate logic]] → [[First-order logic]]''' as the canonical Wave 5 title. “Predicate logic” is historically/common-language terminology but can include or suggest systems beyond strictly first-order quantification. First-order logic is the cleaner modern canonical identity for the intended foundational concept.
* '''[[Consistency]] → [[Consistency (logic)]]''' because unqualified “consistency” has durable non-logical meanings in databases, distributed systems, data, measurement, behavior, and ordinary language.
* [[Contradiction]] remains unqualified because the logical concept is foundational and provides the central general identity, while domain-specific contradictions can qualify later if needed.

No canonical [[Inference]] page is created because [[Inference]] is already complete in Wave 2.

== Domain decision ==

No new controlled Domain is required.

Wave 5 fits the existing controlled vocabulary:

* '''Philosophy''' — logic, argument, reasoning, abduction, belief revision, modality.
* '''Mathematics''' — formal logic, proof, conjecture, probability, distributions, correlation, consistency.
* '''Computer science''' — selected formal-logic and belief-revision applications where substantively relevant.

This wave must not create a redundant “Logic” Domain.

